Long ago, when the world was young, the Sky Goddess Aelara had seven daughters who danced among the clouds. Each daughter wore a gown of a different color—red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, and violet—gifts from the rainbow that had blessed their births.

The daughters danced joyfully by day, but when night fell, they grew lonely in the darkness. They wept silver tears that fell to earth as starlight, but still they yearned for something more.

Seeing her daughters' sadness, Aelara made them a promise. "Dance for me," she said, "and I shall weave your gowns into the night sky itself, so all the world may witness your beauty."

The seven sisters joined hands and spun in a great circle, faster and faster, until their colored gowns began to blur and blend. Aelara reached down and pulled the colors upward, stretching them across the northern heavens like luminous curtains of silk.

